course: dictionary
lesson: 11555
title: Anabolic: building up the body
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to science, and you can work them out by splitting them into parts you know. Anabolic describes building things up in the body. Your body takes small pieces and joins them into bigger ones, the way you build a tower from bricks.
explain: «Growing bodies are very anabolic, building new muscle and bone every day.» Here anabolic tells you the body is busy making bigger things from smaller ones. Muscle and bone are big parts made from many tiny pieces.
explain: Anabolic has an opposite, catabolic, which means breaking bigger things down into smaller ones. Anabolic is building up, and catabolic is breaking down. Think of building a tower and then knocking it down.
explain: «The athlete was banned after a test found anabolic steroids in his blood.» Anabolic steroids are drugs that build muscle. In sport they are cheating, and they can harm your health, so they are banned.
fact: Anabolic means building up bigger molecules from smaller ones in the body.
fact: Anabolic processes include building muscle and helping the body grow.
fact: Catabolic means the opposite: breaking bigger things down into smaller ones.
fact: «Anabolic steroids» are drugs that build muscle.
fact: Using anabolic steroids in sport is cheating and can harm your health.
exercise: «Growing bodies are very anabolic, building new muscle and bone.» What does anabolic mean? | Losing weight quickly | *Building up bigger things from smaller ones | Feeling very tired after sport | Breaking down food into tiny bits
exercise: «The athlete was banned after a test found anabolic steroids in his blood.» Why was he banned? | He was too tall for the team | He forgot his kit | *Using drugs to build muscle is cheating in sport
exercise: In biology, which word is the opposite of anabolic? | Anabolism | Magnetic | *Catabolic | Static
test: Why are anabolic steroids not allowed in sport? | Because they make you grow taller | *Because they are cheating and can harm your health | Because they make you sleepy | Because they are only sweets
test: Which process is anabolic? | *Building muscle and helping the body grow | Breaking down food into energy | Losing water through sweat | Sleeping at night
exam: Anabolic steroids build muscle, so why does using them in sport count as cheating? | Because they only work in winter | Because athletes must eat sweets | *Because they give an unfair boost and can harm health | Because they are made of sugar
